{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cfpma9Sbyxexmh3a1mv8U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Happy to. And I'd start by attacking the criterion most people reach for first, because it's the one that fails worst.\n\n**\"The tests pass\" is nearly circular.** I just wrote seven tests encoding *my* reading of \"alphanumeric.\" I could now write an implementation that turns them all green, and the whole thing would be confidently, uniformly wrong about `café`. Self-written tests passing proves internal consistency, not correctness. They're a necessary floor, never the ceiling — and the greener they are, the more they launder a bad interpretation as finished work.\n\n**Confidence is also the wrong axis.** The intuition \"escalate when you're unsure\" is miscalibrated exactly where it matters. I'm *most* confident where convention is densest — which is precisely where a given project is most likely to have deliberately deviated. And confidence says nothing about stakes.\n\nThe axis I'd actually use is **propagation**: does this choice stay inside the function, or does it escape?\n\nRegex vs. character loop — invisible, reversible, nobody should ever be asked. But `café` → `cafe` vs `caf` vs `café` is a *data format* decision. If slugs get persisted or land in URLs, they end up in links, in bookmarks, in someone's index, and changing it later breaks all of them. That's not a hard technical question — I'd bet on ASCII-with-accent-folding and probably win. It's worth thirty seconds of your attention anyway, because the cost of being wrong is asymmetric and it's cheap to settle now and expensive to settle later.\n\nThe compressed version I'd apply: **if I guess wrong here, who finds out, and when?**\n\n- *I find out immediately* (test fails, type error) → just guess; it's self-correcting.\n- *You find out at review* → guess, but state the assumption so review is cheap.\n- *A user finds out in production — or nobody ever finds out* → escalate.\n\nThat third bucket is the one people forget. Silent wrongness that never surfaces is worse than a crash, because it ships with false assurance attached.\n\n**Now the counter-pressure, which is the real failure mode of this whole framing.** Escalation isn't free, and an agent that asks about everything is worse than one that guesses — it hands the cognitive load back to you while still burning your review time. So the discipline isn't \"ask when unsure.\" It's: do every piece of work that doesn't depend on the answer, then surface the question *once*, batched, with a recommendation already attached. A stated assumption beats a bare question almost every time — \"going with X because Y, say the word\" costs you five seconds to accept, where an open question costs you a decision from scratch. Blocking questions should be reserved for when proceeding wrong would be unsafe or would waste the work.\n\n**One pushback on your framing itself:** \"done\" vs. \"needs a judgment call\" sounds like a binary gate, and treating it that way encourages stopping dead at the first ambiguity. The honest steady state is that most work items are *mostly done with an open question attached*. The useful artifact isn't a verdict — it's a handoff that separates what's settled from what's open.\n\nWhich is why I'd fold one more thing into the definition of done: **an accurate account of what you didn't do.** Finishing 90% and quietly dropping 10% isn't 90% done; it's a worse object than that, because you don't know which 10% is missing. Scaling scope down is your call, not mine.\n\nThe place I'm genuinely unsure: whether any of this survives being written down as a rule. A standing \"check before proceeding\" step degrades into rubber-stamping fast — you'd get the cost of escalation with none of the signal, since the only thing that makes a raised hand meaningful is that it's rare. Do you want this as something enforceable, or just as a shared instinct about when to interrupt you?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9835,"cache_read_input_tokens":12800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9835},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ee6ecf6a-81f4-40d9-90f3-54c3d29d9f88","uuid":"bec90c9d-2103-45ad-9cf3-95c82ec6fefc","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:28:49.658Z","request_id":"req_011Cfpma9AE78CR78RVCFkYY"}
